// A whole K65 program, part one: the declarations.
//
// Written for this corpus rather than copied from anywhere.  Unlike the
// single-claim fixtures beside it, what this one is for is the *combination* —
// the way a real source mixes constructs that the other fixtures isolate.
// `fixture.txt` lists them.
//
// The TIA register names come from the A2600 system script, which the original
// compiler runs before the first unit (`workdir/system_a2600.nut` in the K65
// checkout), so nothing declares them here.

bank core

// A comma list with an address on the first name and the `?` marker on the
// last: three consecutive bytes at $80, $81, $82, and one compile-time line
// saying where `phase` landed.
var frame = 0x80, cursor, phase?

inline wsync   { WSYNC = a }
inline blank   { VBLANK = a = 2 }
inline unblank { VBLANK = a = 0 }
